<title>GERMANY: Deutsche - politics obstructed Thyssen bid.</title>
<headline>Deutsche - politics obstructed Thyssen bid.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank chairman Hilmar Kopper said on Wednesday that the aborted takeover bid by Krupp for Thyssen AG was made impossible by politics.</p>
<p>&quot;The thing fell down as a result of political intervention,&quot; Kopper said. Deutsche was holding its annual news conference detailing 1996 results.</p>
<p>&quot;It remains to be seen whether Thyssen and its staff will be better off with the solution now being drawn up than with an outright takeover,&quot; he said, referring to the two companies plans for a steel joint venture.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
